{"records":[{"id":"m9c8ysryzb","title":"Metabolic classification for enzymatic reactions present in the ten Cancer-Hallmarks of Homo sapiens and Arabidopsis thalina","description":"When performing the identification and metabolic classification of the genes that code for proteins with exclusive catalytic activity involved in Cancer-Hallmarks genes (CHG) and cancer development for each species; 1297 genes for H. sapiens (SD3) and 609 genes for A. thaliana (SD4) were found. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-11-18T22:05:19.558Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/m9c8ysryzb","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/m9c8ysryzb"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Diana Carolina","last_name":"Clavijo Buriticá","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Bioinformatics","Systems Biology","Cancer","Metabolism"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xdnrtw7kpb","title":"Predicting Prostate Adenocarcinoma Patients’ Survival and Immune Signature: A Novel Risk Model Based on Telomere-Related Genes. Jief Zheng, Jiah Chen et al.","description":"Telomere-related genes (TRGs) play an essential role in the carcinogenesis and progression of prostate adenocarcinoma（PRAD）. The prognostic value of TRGs remains unclear in PRAD. We conducted a study using The Cancer Genome Atlas-Prostate Adenocarcinoma (TCGA-PRAD) dataset as the training group and the Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center (MSKCC) and Gene Expression Omnibus (GEO) datasets as the validation group. We developed a risk model and a nomogram to predict survival rates in patients with PRAD. The expression of model genes and their possible regulatory mechanisms were then analyzed. Furthermore, we explored the relationship between the risk model and immune cell infiltration, chemotherapy drug sensitivity, and specific signaling pathways using the CIBERSORT algorithm, the Genomics of Drug Sensitivity in Cancer (GDSC) database, and motif enrichment. The integrated nomogram can be a good predictor of 3- and 5-year survival in patients with PRAD. This risk model is valuable for guiding the selection of immunotherapy and chemotherapy in the clinical treatment of patients with PRAD.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-08-13T06:19:34.142Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xdnrtw7kpb","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xdnrtw7kpb"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jiahui","last_name":"Chen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Prostate Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"4s638rfv2x","title":"Bibliometrix-Export-File","description":"Raw bibliometric dataset for the manuscript \"Mapping the Evolutionary Landscape of Cancer Immunotherapy: A Global Bibliometric Analysis of Cancer Immunotherapy Trends in Solid Tumors Over a Quarter Century (2000–2025)\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-06-30T04:06:24.073Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4s638rfv2x","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4s638rfv2x"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Ender Eren","last_name":"Özçelik","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Bibliometrics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"wpw7mstpp8","title":"Gene sequencing of a rare mutant lung cancer","description":"This sequencing contains 73 genes associated with the occurrence and development of lung cancer, including important genes related to targeted therapy and drug resistance such as BRAF, ALK, RET, ROS1, MET, EGFR, KRAS, ERBB2 in the NCCN guidelines, as well as genes related to PD-1/PD-L1 immunotherapy such as MLH1, MSH2, MSH6, PMS2, POLE, and genes related to chemotherapy drug toxicity and efficacy.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-09-01T15:15:22.885Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/wpw7mstpp8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/wpw7mstpp8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":" FANGFANG ","last_name":"WANG","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Gene Sequencing"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3ypwdz6ygs","title":"TEAD functions as a conserved master regulator of DNA repair systems: Implications for cancer immunotherapy ","description":"This dataset accompanies the manuscript “TEAD functions as a conserved master regulator of DNA repair systems: Implications for cancer immunotherapy.” We hypothesize that TEAD transcription factors coordinate DNA-repair programs and that TEAD1/4 perturbation reshapes genome instability and tumor immunogenicity. The dataset includes multi-omics and molecular profiling resources generated in mouse colorectal cancer CT26 cells: TEAD CUT&Tag peak identification (Table 1), RNA-seq transcriptional profiling of Tead1/4 double-KO versus parental cells (Table 2), curated TEAD1/4 target genes (Table 3), TEAD1/4-associated proteins identified by mass spectrometry (Table 4), RNA-seq after Setd1a knockdown (Table 5), ATAC-seq chromatin accessibility landscapes (Table 6), and lists of novel nonsynonymous SNVs/indels and NetMHCcons-predicted neoantigens in Tead1/4 double-KO cells (Tables 7–8). RNA sequence information (siRNA and primer sequences) is provided (Tables 9–10). These files enable integrative analysis of TEAD-dependent chromatin regulation, transcription, protein interactions, and mutation/neoantigen consequences relevant to immunotherapy.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-12-25T03:20:56.455Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3ypwdz6ygs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3ypwdz6ygs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jiahong","last_name":"Duan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Yicheng","last_name":"Ma","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Chenggang","last_name":"Zou","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["RNA Sequencing","Mass Measurement","ATAC-Seq"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"9285c3hzmh","title":"Pan-cancer analysis of the role of NCS1 in immunotherapy and prognosis of human cancer","description":"Pan-cancer analysis of the role of NCS1 in immunotherapy and prognosis of human cancer","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-10-18T19:39:58.971Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9285c3hzmh","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9285c3hzmh"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Genchun","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"kai","last_name":"sun","orcid":null},{"first_name":"zhou","last_name":"guo","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Fengjing","last_name":"Guo","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Oncology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"mpkbbc367j","title":"Novel radiation-derived gene blueprint stratifying patients with breast cancer","description":"Breast cancer (BC) is a prevalent global malignancy with a high recurrence rate. The effectiveness of predictive, preventive, and personalized treatment strategies is limited by a lack of reliable prognostic biomarkers. Radiotherapy significantly reduces breast cancer recurrence risk and prolongs patients’ lives. However, the role of radiation-related genes in breast cancer remains unclear.Differentially expressed radiation-related genes were identified through analysis of the BRCA gene expression matrix between radiation and non-radiation groups. Multi-omics investigation, including bulk and single-cell RNA sequencing, was conducted to explore these genes in breast cancer. A risk model was developed using random forest, stepAIC, and LASSO Cox regression analyses to predict prognosis, immune cell infiltration, immunotherapy response, and targeted drug sensitivity based on radiation-related gene expression profiles. Functional differences were assessed via Kyoto Encyclopedia of Genes and Genomes (KEGG) pathway and Gene Ontology (GO) enrichment analyses. We identified 133 radiation-related differentially expressed genes (DEGs), with 26 hub genes selected via LASSO and random forest models. Single-cell analysis revealed enrichment of radiation-related scores primarily in malignant cells. The radiation-related risk model, validated in the METABRIC dataset and an independent prognostic indicator in the TCGA-BRCA cohort, showed that low-risk patients had higher overall survival rates than high-risk patients. Risk scores correlated with immune infiltration, and low-risk patients exhibited greater immunotherapy response based on immune checkpoint gene expression. Drug sensitivity to gemcitabine, lapatinib, methotrexate, and doxorubicin varied across risk groups. To put it briefly, a strong efficient risk model was created to forecast prognosis, TME features, reactions to immunotherapy targeted medications in BRCA. This might lead to new understandings of individualized accurate treatment approaches. To facilitate clinical application, we have developed an R package and Excel-based calculator tool that enables clinicians to easily calculate patient risk scores using the 8-gene signature. These tools, along with detailed usage instructions, are freely available in the supplementary materials and GitHub repository.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-08-18T19:16:41.558Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/mpkbbc367j","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/mpkbbc367j"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Hao","last_name":"Zhang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Honghua","last_name":"Lin","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Dong","last_name":"Shi","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Enyi","last_name":"Qiu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wenqi","last_name":"Jin","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Breast Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"9zn66k84n8","title":"Apatinib remodels the immunosuppressive tumor ecosystem of gastric cancer enhancing anti-PD-1 immunotherapy","description":"Apatinib has been shown to clinically enhance anti-PD-1 immunotherapy for advanced gastric cancer (GC). However, the complexity of GC immunosuppression remains a challenge for precision immunotherapy. Here, we profiled the transcriptomes of 34,182 single cells from GC patient-derived xenografts of humanized mouse models treated with vehicle, nivolumab, or nivolumab plus apatinib. Notably, excessive expression of CXCL5 in CellCycle malignant epithelium, induced by anti-PD-1 immunotherapy and blocked by combined apatinib treatment, was found to be a key driver of tumor-associated neutrophil (TAN) recruitment in tumor microenvironment through the CXCL5/CXCR2 axis. We further revealed that the protumor TAN signature was associated with anti-PD-1 immunotherapy-related progressive disease and poor cancer prognosis. Molecular and functional analyses in cell-derived xenograft models directly confirmed the positive in vivo therapeutic effect of targeting CXCL5/CXCR2 axis during anti-PD-1 immunotherapy. Altogether, our study elucidates GC immunosuppressive landscape in anti-PD-1 immunotherapy and highlights potential targets for overcoming checkpoint immunotherapy resistance.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-03-27T14:03:00.915Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9zn66k84n8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9zn66k84n8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Wangyu","last_name":"Cai","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer Immunotherapy","Stomach Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"j8sd6kpy22","title":"A 16-hour fasting optimizes cancer immunotherapy in mice and humans","description":"Source data for “16-h fasting optimizes cancer immunotherapy in mice and humans”","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-10-29T09:27:10.862Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/j8sd6kpy22","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/j8sd6kpy22"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Di","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Tumor Immunology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"jvd46cfsjc","title":"Disparities in immunotherapy treatment for mycosis fungoides and Sézary syndrome in the National Cancer Database","description":"Supplementary materials for \"Disparities in immunotherapy treatment for mycosis fungoides and Sézary syndrome in the National Cancer Database\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-10-17T14:20:59.077Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/jvd46cfsjc","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/jvd46cfsjc"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Bryan","last_name":"Peacker","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Dermatology","Immunotherapy","Cutaneous T-Cell Lymphoma","Health Disparity"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":136701,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":150,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":136701,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":136056,"restricted":68,"embargoed":577},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2253},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":1338},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":662},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Centre","count":463},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":432},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":412},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":402},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":380},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":330},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":268}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":134066},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1902},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":182},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":135},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":78},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f84e575e4","name":"Digital Commons Data@Becker","count":66},{"id":"72c28c45-627f-446b-8a48-af7c0a51a357","name":"Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore","count":55},{"id":"b121dfec-bb51-4f19-a2f6-bc9ce0197286","name":"Babeș-Bolyai University","count":40},{"id":"7e51a2dd-133e-43c6-a220-12c1958e202a","name":"University of Canberra","count":31},{"id":"f2ed6517-7fb4-4e02-8cef-95e75e9f0c9d","name":"Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University","count":28}],"top_institutions_stats":[{"id":"ecb64011-71f0-5223-b4e4-4d27d5f51d83","name":"Universidad Autonoma de Madrid Centro de Biologia Molecular Severo Ochoa","count":867},{"id":"9d63ad1d-c391-5c35-a12e-cafe17017098","name":"Universidad Autonoma de Madrid","count":761},{"id":"3bfef41a-d03e-5722-bd55-dd245235fa78","name":"Bina Nusantara University","count":421},{"id":"0ad97c43-5173-56e6-bbe6-46dad5323862","name":"Daffodil International University","count":409},{"id":"55ba66b2-f276-5204-a3d8-acfa499794e0","name":"The University of Manchester","count":359}]}}